From: Andreas Ziegler <dev@andreas-ziegler.de>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 02:54:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mesh: match kernel 2.4 GHz default basic rates for unencrypted mesh

When mesh_basic_rates is not explicitly configured on 2.4 GHz
(HOSTAPD_MODE_IEEE80211G), wpa_supplicant_mesh_init() unconditionally
overrides bss->conf->basic_rates with basic_rates_erp (1, 2, 5.5, 6, 11,
12, 24 Mbps). Unencrypted kernel-managed 802.11s meshes (such as `iw dev ...
mesh join`, OpenWrt <= 22.03, and wpad-basic-* setups) rely on Linux
cfg80211 __cfg80211_join_mesh(), which defaults on 2.4 GHz to 1 Mbps
only as the sole basic rate for backward compatibility. Strict basic-rate
matching in mac80211 causes peering failure between wpa_supplicant and
kernel-MPM nodes.

Keep the basic_rates_erp override when mesh security is enabled
(preserving backward compatibility with existing SAE encrypted meshes),
and use { 10, 0 } (1 Mbps) for unencrypted 2.4 GHz meshes so both
beacons and peering frames match Linux cfg80211's default basic rates.

Ref: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/15826
Signed-off-by: Andreas Ziegler <dev@andreas-ziegler.de>
---
 wpa_supplicant/mesh.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/wpa_supplicant/mesh.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/mesh.c
@@ -367,6 +367,7 @@ static int wpa_supplicant_mesh_init(stru
 	struct hostapd_config *conf;
 	struct mesh_conf *mconf;
 	int basic_rates_erp[] = { 10, 20, 55, 60, 110, 120, 240, 0 };
+	int basic_rates_open[] = { 10, 0 };
 	int frequency;
 	bool is_dfs;
 	u8 chan;
@@ -529,9 +530,14 @@ static int wpa_supplicant_mesh_init(stru
 		 * advertised in beacons match the one in peering frames, sigh.
 		 */
 		if (conf->hw_mode == HOSTAPD_MODE_IEEE80211G) {
-			bss->conf->basic_rates = os_memdup(
-				basic_rates_erp,
-				sizeof(basic_rates_erp));
+			if (mconf->security != MESH_CONF_SEC_NONE)
+				bss->conf->basic_rates = os_memdup(
+					basic_rates_erp,
+					sizeof(basic_rates_erp));
+			else
+				bss->conf->basic_rates = os_memdup(
+					basic_rates_open,
+					sizeof(basic_rates_open));
 			if (!bss->conf->basic_rates)
 				goto out_free;
 		}
